<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Random Chore Picker | Household Task Selector</title><meta name="description" content="Add household chores and randomly choose the next task. A simple free chore selector for families, housemates and personal routines."><meta name="robots" content="index,follow"><link rel="canonical" href="https://wheelnamepicker.com.au/chore-picker"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/value-pages.css"></head><body><div class="top"><div class="nav"><a class="brand" href="/">Wheel Name Picker</a><div class="links"><a href="/activity-picker">Activity Picker</a><a href="/dinner-picker">Dinner Picker</a><a href="/yes-no-picker">Yes/No Picker</a></div></div></div><header class="hero"><span class="badge">Household helper</span><h1>Random Chore Picker</h1><p>Put the jobs that actually need doing into one list and let the picker choose the next task. Remove completed chores as you go, or keep them in the pool for repeat routines.</p></header><main class="wrap"><div class="tool"><div class="grid"><div class="field"><label for="chores">Chores</label><textarea id="chores">Wash dishes
Fold laundry
Sweep floor
Wipe benches
Take bins out
Tidy lounge room</textarea></div><div class="field"><label for="mode">After picking</label><select id="mode"><option value="remove">Remove completed chore</option><option value="keep">Keep chore in the list</option></select><div class="actions"><button id="pick">Choose a chore</button><button class="secondary" id="reset">Restore example list</button></div></div></div><div class="result big-choice" id="result">Ready</div></div><div class="article"><section><h2>Turn a vague cleaning list into one next step</h2><p>A long list of jobs can feel harder than a single clear action. The chore picker does not create a schedule or judge priority; it simply narrows your current list to one randomly selected task. That makes it useful for casual household routines, shared cleanup sessions or moments when nobody wants to decide what comes first.</p></section><section><h2>Make the list realistic</h2><p>Add tasks that are small enough to start immediately. “Clean the whole house” is usually too broad, while “wipe kitchen benches” or “put away one load of laundry” gives the picker something concrete to choose. You can also include short reset jobs such as refilling pet water, clearing a table or putting shoes away.</p></section><section><h2>Ideas for families and housemates</h2><ul><li>Build a list only from jobs that are appropriate for everyone taking part.</li><li>Use the picker during a 15-minute shared reset rather than as a punishment.</li><li>Remove completed jobs so the list shrinks visibly.</li><li>Create separate lists for kitchen, outdoor, bedroom or weekly jobs.</li></ul></section><section><h2>Random is not the same as fair workload</h2><p>If different jobs take very different amounts of time, a random picker can produce uneven effort. For a shared household, it may be better to keep similarly sized tasks in one list or agree on time limits. Accessibility, age and capability also matter; the person using the tool should decide which chores belong in the pool.</p></section><section><h2>Keep routines flexible</h2><p>The picker is deliberately lightweight. Nothing is saved to an account, and the page works entirely in the browser. If you need a long-term recurring roster, use a calendar or dedicated task manager. If you just need one job chosen right now, this page keeps the decision small.</p></section></div></main><footer class="footer"><a href="/about">About</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a><a href="/terms">Terms</a><a href="/contact/">Contact</a><p>© 2026 Wheel Name Picker · Ascension Digital Group</p></footer><script>const $=id=>document.getElementById(id),sample='Wash dishes\nFold laundry\nSweep floor\nWipe benches\nTake bins out\nTidy lounge room';function items(){return $('chores').value.split(/\n|,/).map(x=>x.trim()).filter(Boolean)}$('pick').onclick=()=>{const a=items();if(!a.length)return $('result').textContent='Add at least one chore.';const i=Math.floor(Math.random()*a.length),v=a[i];$('result').textContent=v;if($('mode').value==='remove'){a.splice(i,1);$('chores').value=a.join('\n')}};$('reset').onclick=()=>{$('chores').value=sample;$('result').textContent='Ready'};</script></body></html>